{{root|lt|ine-pro|*h₃emh₃-}}
Attestations with the meaning “power, consciousness” support a connection with {{cog|sa|अम||tr=áma-|strength}}, {{cog|ae|𐬇𐬨𐬀||attacking power, strength, potence}}<ref>Rolandas Kregždys (2002) [http://www.baltistica.lt/index.php/baltistica/article/download/721/660 Dėl lie. ãmas] [Concerning lit. ãmas]. ''Baltistica'', volume 37, number 2, pages 269-272</ref>; From {{cog|ine-pro|*h₃emh₃-||take hold of; be strong}}. This root has been connected with {{cog|grc|ὄμνυμι||swear}}, {{cog|sa|अमन्ति||tr=amánti|take hold of, swear}}, and most likely {{cog|la|amō||love}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL}}</ref>

Must be separated from {{m|lt|ãmalioti||talk nonsense}}, of [[onomatopoeia|onomatopoeic]] origin. See {{m|lt|am̃sėti||yap, yelp}}.

